{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Oholibamah daughter of Anah.</b> She was of the sons of Seir the Horite, and through her Esau went to the land of Seir, as it says: <b>So Esau settled in Mount Seir</b>, and his sons after him destroyed the Horite, as it says: כַּאֲשֶׁר עָשָׂה לִבְנֵי עֵשָׂו הַיּוֹשְׁבִים בְּשֵׂעִיר אֲשֶׁר הִשְׁמִיד אֶת הַחוֹרִי מִפְּנֵיהֶם (Deuteronomy 2:12). Therefore he went back and said: <b>And these are the generations of Esau the father of Edom in Mount Seir</b>. And he listed the chiefs (alufim) because his sons after him conquered, and Timna became a concubine, and the generations of Esau became chiefs (alufim)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:29.256244733Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}